{
  "version": 2,
  "storage": "Existing TEXT, one canonical citation per LF line; original legacy scalar remains readable.",
  "semantics": "Each comma group is OR, ampersand within a group is AND. Ancestors include paragraphs/items, but 조의/호의 are distinct. Missing-law token is __없음__. Search ('cases') may split ',' and '&'; a query equal to one stored key matches it whole. Stored-key membership ('key_cases', web lawExact=true, mobile ReportFilter.lawExact, stats law filter) never splits: one key per line = AND, a row belongs to K when one of its keys is K or a descendant paragraph/item. Text that is not one structured key (law name containing ',', '&' or another N조) stays one raw key with its spacing. Each per-law statistic bar count equals key membership of its filter ('stats_cases').",
